                        "word": "megalopolitan"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "4388ee94-a6c1-3d62-9088-c976085a297d",
                "word": "Megapolitan",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8ea94166-daaa-309e-a8d5-39c8acbc81e2",
                        "entry_id": "4388ee94-a6c1-3d62-9088-c976085a297d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, pertaining to, or from the ancient city of Megalopolis (now Megalopoli) in Greece."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "18d8833f-4e37-41ca-9f92-8b36b08f1c5e",
                                "sense_id": "8ea94166-daaa-309e-a8d5-39c8acbc81e2",
                                "text": "At length he [Antigonus III Doson] assaulted with his right wing the position of Eucleidas; and, favoured by an error of that general, and a timely charge of Philopœmen with the Megapolitan cavalry, gained a complete victory."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0389c76b-6a96-457b-b1ba-765e2e1b9d08",
                                "sense_id": "8ea94166-daaa-309e-a8d5-39c8acbc81e2",
                                "text": "The upshot is, we are guided by a party of shock-headed Arcadians, who are going in the direction of the excavations, and a Megapolitan boy who has probably an eye to gain."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "bde33fac-f560-4fc0-9612-930c313cd07a",
                        "source_entry_id": "4388ee94-a6c1-3d62-9088-c976085a297d",
                        "source_sense_ids": [
                            "8ea94166-daaa-309e-a8d5-39c8acbc81e2"
                        ],
                        "linkage_type": "synonyms",
                        "word": "Megalopolitan"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "ae51e52e-c1ff-362b-bbde-cf88f5793fb9",
                "word": "megapolitan",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4203aed1-4ae7-4c52-8ca2-1f8b3a6c60cb",
                        "entry_id": "ae51e52e-c1ff-362b-bbde-cf88f5793fb9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "megapolitans"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37e46fec-a508-34f2-85e0-058e8ce5be2c",
                        "entry_id": "ae51e52e-c1ff-362b-bbde-cf88f5793fb9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of megapolis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e28c7e4-5893-4a99-aa7b-f19ade7d649f",
                                "sense_id": "37e46fec-a508-34f2-85e0-058e8ce5be2c",
                                "text": "With developments already planned, within 20 years Buckeye is expected to become a metropolis nearly as large as Phoenix. And Phoenix will be expanding east and south, too, creating a Phoenix/Tucson megapolitan. A total of such 10 megapolitans with urban and residential construction linking today's central cities into new, huge megapolitans: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ed1f2de-a9ef-48d2-8eca-c8620ff9f250",
                                "sense_id": "37e46fec-a508-34f2-85e0-058e8ce5be2c",
                                "text": "In the United States, trans-metropolitan areas are referred to as megapolitans, large urban regions with physically interconnected metropolitan and micropolitan areas through transportation networks, constituting a functionally interdependent urban network[…]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4856d148-ce78-3be7-af23-6bed8545b102",
                        "entry_id": "ae51e52e-c1ff-362b-bbde-cf88f5793fb9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An inhabitant of a megapolis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
